.Dd January 29, 2026
.Dt BC 1
.Os Substrate
.Sh NAME
.Nm bc
.Nd arbitrary precision calculator language
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl h
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is an arbitrary precision calculator language interpreter.
It supports standard POSIX bc features as well as several GNU extensions.
.Pp
The calculator supports numbers with arbitrary precision, limited only by available memory.
.Sh EXTENSIONS
.Nm
implements the following GNU extensions:
.Bl -tag -width "Comments"
.It Comments
Support for
.Li #
characters to start a comment that extends to the end of the line.
.It Control Flow
Support for
.Li if (cond) { ... } else { ... }
syntax, allowing full structured programming.
.It Input/Output
The
.Li print
statement allows printing a list of strings and expressions, separated by commas.
For example:
.Li print "Value: ", a, "\n"
.It Variables
Multi-character variable names are supported (e.g.,
.Li myVar = 10
).
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr dc 1
.Sh HISTORY
This implementation of
.Nm
was written for the Substrate operating system.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Segin
